&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is Saudi&#39;s first fintech unicorn and is backed by Sanabil Investments, SNB Capital, Checkout.com, amongst others, operating out its headquarters in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia with other regional and global support offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Customer Care Manager to lead UAE customer care from our Cairo site. This is a role for a strong leader who manages through Team Leaders but knows the operation cold — someone who leads with full context and credibility, never secondhand. You won&#39;t get blocked by operational detail, you won&#39;t lean on your team to understand your own numbers, and you&#39;ll contribute substantively to how the operation runs. You own the effectiveness and performance of the UAE Customer Care Team. You set the standard and hold the team to it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Leadership &amp;amp; Performance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic to the Team Leaders, overseeing the daily output and supervision of operational performance to ensure interactions reflect positively on the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns department KPIs, including service level agreements, average handling time, customer satisfaction,..etc. and read the raw contact-center and survey data yourself, well enough to know what&#39;s happening without being told.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage performance and identify gaps, and drive resolution at the team level&amp;nbsp; coaching, reslotting, queue and workflow adjustments within your operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Assurance &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Quality Assurance and Training Teams to oversee onboarding training, continuous coaching, and upskilling for better service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the ultimate escalation point for complex or sensitive UAE customer grievances, resolving issues with high ownership and speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and analyze customer surveys to gather structured data and research customer opinions of services and the team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Development &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a highly motivated team, and high retention culture through transparent performance management, coaching, and regular feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured performance reviews with Team Leaders, nurturing their leadership capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead recruitment activities to build a top tier talent pool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile &amp;amp; Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading managers and Team Leaders in a high-volume, fast-paced, multi-channel customer care operation — ideally owning a contact-center operation end-to-end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on operational fluency: you operate the tools, read the data, and know the workflows yourself — a credible operator who leads, not a delegator who relies on the team for context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced hands-on experience with modern CRM, telephony, and channel tools (e.g., Zendesk, Salesforce). Strong capability utilizing data visualization tools to track metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven, emotionally intelligent leader capable of program-managing critical structural changes while maintaining high team morale across an offshore site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to interpret raw contact center analytics and survey data into actionable performance improvement plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar across the board - from your own contributions to the people you work with to the tools you work on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail &amp;amp; project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance attention to detail with swift execution - we need to do things quickly, and we need to do them well. Juggling those can be challenging, and this should be a strength&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is the leading fintech platform to shop, pay, and bank in Saudi Arabia and the wider GCC region, and Saudi’s first fintech unicorn. Tamara’s mission is to empower people in their daily lives and revolutionize how they shop, pay, and bank. Tamara serves millions of users in KSA, UAE, and Kuwait, and partners with leading global and regional brands such as SHEIN, Jarir, noon, IKEA, eXtra, and Farfetch, as well as thousands of SMEs. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, SNB Capital, and Checkout.com, amongst others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Care Trainer is responsible for delivering training programs that equip Customer and Partner Care teams with the knowledge, skills, and confidence required to provide excellent service.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role plays a key part in onboarding new hires, reinforcing operational knowledge, and supporting continuous learning across the Care organization. The trainer works closely with the Training Design team and Operations to ensure training delivery is effective, engaging, and aligned with operational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver instructor-led training sessions for new hires and existing Customer Care teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate training on product knowledge, systems, workflows, customer/partner service skills, communication techniques, company policies, and new company launches for products/features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure sessions are engaging, interactive, and aligned with learning objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onboarding Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate onboarding training for new Care representatives, ensuring they are equipped with the knowledge and operational understanding required to begin handling customer interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the transition from training to the operational environment by reinforcing key processes and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Reinforcement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct refresher sessions and targeted training to address knowledge gaps or operational updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce key concepts through coaching, practical exercises, and scenario-based learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Effectiveness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather feedback from participants and stakeholders to evaluate training effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share observations and improvement opportunities with the Training Design team to enhance future training programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Content Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure training materials from the Training Design team are used consistently and stay up to date during delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag outdated or unclear materials to the Training Design team for review and updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration with Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Operations leaders and SMEs to stay aligned with process updates, product changes, and operational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure training delivery reflects current operational practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality &amp;amp; Coaching Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observe customer interactions where relevant to identify learning opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback and reinforcement to support applying training in the live environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Learning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed about product updates, process changes, and service standards to ensure accurate training delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve facilitation techniques to enhance learner engagement and knowledge retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;2–3 years of experience in a full-time training role within customer support, partner support, customer service, or a related environment.&lt;strong&gt; TOT certification&lt;/strong&gt; is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training and Development Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong training and development skills are essential. This includes the ability to deliver and implement effective training programs, assess training needs, and evaluate training effectiveness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written, are critical for a trainer. They must be able to effectively convey information and instructions to trainees, as well as communicate with colleagues and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer/ Partner Care Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; A deep understanding of customer service principles and best practices is essential. Care trainers should be able to coach trainees on how to handle various interactions, resolve issues efficiently, and maintain a positive customer/partner experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong organizational skills are necessary to manage training schedules, materials, and resources effectively. Care trainers often juggle multiple tasks and responsibilities, so the ability to prioritize and manage time efficiently is crucial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to adapt to changing priorities, technologies, and business processes is important in a fast-paced Care environment. Care trainers should be flexible and able to quickly adjust training programs as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an early to mid career Data Analyst (min 3 years experience) to take us to the next stage of growth, supporting the finance function. The successful candidate will have experience developing analytical solutions and assisting with data-driven decision making, while managing stakeholders from finance and corporate finance. You will be at the confluence of finance and data, helping to shape financial reporting with a solid understanding of accounting and finance paired with practical experience working on databases, ETL/ELT processes, and building dashboards. Tamara is a high growth startup looking to develop key product success metrics and enhancing decision making through data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive business impact through actionable insights and identifying key opportunities for rapid growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards that provide accurate and actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the data engineering team on the data enrichment needs of the product team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with stakeholders across the business to prioritize projects based on impact and drive&lt;br&gt;delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing a process to identify, analyse, and interpret trends or patterns in complex data sets,&lt;br&gt;empower informed decision making for stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring governance and being a steward of good analytical practices throughout the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Ideal Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in financial data analysis, with a preference for experience in the BNPL industry or a related field. Demonstrating understanding of the unique data and financial metrics relevant to BNPL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Financial modeling, data manipulation using SQL, and potentially programming languages like Python or R.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Visualization:&lt;/strong&gt; Creating clear and insightful data visualizations like dashboards and reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Knowledge and Analysis Techniques:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Budgeting and Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience in working with financial budgets and forecasts, using data analysis to inform projections and identify potential risks or opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Statement Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Expertise in analyzing financial statements to assess a company&#39;s health, performance, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cost Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience in analyzing business operation costs and identifying cost optimization opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BNPL Products and Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with various BNPL products (e.g., point-of-sale financing, virtual cards) and the financial metrics used to evaluate their performance (e.g., approval rates, conversion rates, delinquency, recovery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Markets and Instruments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding of:&lt;/strong&gt; Equity markets, debt markets, derivatives markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debt Securitization Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Knowledge of debt securitization structures, tranching analysis, and performance metrics used to evaluate securitized BNPL debt instruments (e.g., credit enhancement levels, loss severities).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial Regulations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Awareness of relevant financial regulations:&lt;/strong&gt; GAAP, IFRS, or industry-specific regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Desirable Qualities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience managing and cleaning large datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-solving and Critical Thinking:&lt;/strong&gt; Tackling complex financial problems through data analysis and translating them into actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal communication to present findings and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to lead or participate in cross-functional projects, collaborating effectively with various departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Identifying key financial metrics that drive profitability and growth, along with commercial awareness of the industry and competitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager II&lt;/strong&gt; to lead a critical area of our engineering organization. In this role, you will be accountable for the delivery and technical strategy across multiple complex and related domains within our product. You will lead a high-performing team of 6-10 senior engineers, potentially structured across two squads, driving the execution of team-level goals that are directly aligned with broader organizational priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing on your deep expertise in software development and proven leadership, you will guide the architectural evolution of your team&#39;s systems, ensuring they are reliable, scalable, and performant. You will be a key partner to product and business leadership, influencing medium- and long-term strategy and ensuring your teams are focused on delivering measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your ultimate responsibility is to orchestrate technical excellence, foster the growth of senior engineers and future leaders, manage complex cross-team dependencies, and transform how millions of users engage in shopping, payment, and banking activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a driven, determined, and curious leader, who knows that collective strength means we all win. With a positive outlook, you are solution-oriented–persevering regardless of circumstances, always finding a way through, no matter the challenges. You will effectively find a way to work with everyone through empathy and respect. You will be driven and comfortable with responding quickly with urgency, with the ability to change course without losing momentum and energy, resulting in great success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspire and guide a group of senior engineers, setting a clear direction that aligns with the company vision. Drive alignment between technology goals and product priorities, advocating for long-term technical quality alongside short-term delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership &amp;amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop both direct reports and skip-levels for future leadership roles. Create growth opportunities for senior engineers, mentor those aspiring to become Engineering Manager I&#39;s, and support the success of new managers. Drive team structure decisions, hiring plans, and succession planning while effectively managing performance across all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead architectural discussions for your team&#39;s systems. Drive continuous improvements to system reliability, performance, and scalability. Monitor technical health and ensure the team maintains a healthy balance between new feature delivery and technical investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and own the delivery plans for initiatives that span multiple teams. Own resource allocation and hiring strategy for your area. Proactively identify and resolve complex cross-team delivery challenges, making strategic trade-offs between short- and long-term value. Provide clear visibility to leadership on project status, risks, and mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Business Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with Product and business leadership to influence medium- and long-term product strategies. Ensure your teams are focusing on measurable outcomes and ROI, and encourage a culture of thoughtful experimentation aligned with strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Health &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Build a healthy, inclusive environment of trust, ownership, and accountability. Foster a strong collaboration and knowledge-sharing culture. Work closely with peer Engineering Managers and the architecture board to ensure alignment and drive standards across the engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least &lt;strong&gt;4+ years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; managing one or more engineering teams, with a proven track record of managing senior individual contributors and leading projects of medium-to-high complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning delivery for &lt;strong&gt;initiatives spanning multiple teams or complex product domains.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background in modern software development (e.g., Java/Go, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Messaging Queues, Cloud Services), with experience &lt;strong&gt;leading architectural discussions and driving technical strategy.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with product managers to &lt;strong&gt;influence product roadmaps and align technical strategy with business objectives.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop engineering talent, including &lt;strong&gt;mentoring senior engineers and aspiring managers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Agile methodologies and experience resolving complex, cross-team delivery challenges in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech or eCommerce experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

