&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership &amp;amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop both direct reports and skip-levels for future leadership roles. Create growth opportunities for senior engineers, mentor those aspiring to become Engineering Manager I&#39;s, and support the success of new managers. Drive team structure decisions, hiring plans, and succession planning while effectively managing performance across all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead architectural discussions for your team&#39;s systems. Drive continuous improvements to system reliability, performance, and scalability. Monitor technical health and ensure the team maintains a healthy balance between new feature delivery and technical investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and own the delivery plans for initiatives that span multiple teams. Own resource allocation and hiring strategy for your area. Proactively identify and resolve complex cross-team delivery challenges, making strategic trade-offs between short- and long-term value. Provide clear visibility to leadership on project status, risks, and mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Business Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with Product and business leadership to influence medium- and long-term product strategies. Ensure your teams are focusing on measurable outcomes and ROI, and encourage a culture of thoughtful experimentation aligned with strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Health &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Build a healthy, inclusive environment of trust, ownership, and accountability. Foster a strong collaboration and knowledge-sharing culture. Work closely with peer Engineering Managers and the architecture board to ensure alignment and drive standards across the engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least &lt;strong&gt;4+ years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; managing one or more engineering teams, with a proven track record of managing senior individual contributors and leading projects of medium-to-high complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning delivery for &lt;strong&gt;initiatives spanning multiple teams or complex product domains.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background in modern software development (e.g., Java/Go, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Messaging Queues, Cloud Services), with experience &lt;strong&gt;leading architectural discussions and driving technical strategy.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with product managers to &lt;strong&gt;influence product roadmaps and align technical strategy with business objectives.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to develop engineering talent, including &lt;strong&gt;mentoring senior engineers and aspiring managers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in Agile methodologies and experience resolving complex, cross-team delivery challenges in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fintech or eCommerce experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others. operating out of its headquarters in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia with other regional and global support offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your Role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Financial Reporting specialist, you&#39;re the maestro behind our financial harmony. Your&amp;nbsp;mission is to nail the accuracy, transparency, and compliance of our financial reporting,&amp;nbsp;crafting financial reports and disclosures in compliance with international accounting&amp;nbsp;standards and best practices. We are all about collaboration here, so team up with our internal&amp;nbsp;squads, analyze financial data and freely apply your strong analytical skills. A keen attention&amp;nbsp;to detail, profound understanding of accounting standards, and proficiency in financial&amp;nbsp;modelling are integral to this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1) Financial Reporting &amp;amp; Consolidation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Prepare accurate and timely financial reports and disclosures in compliance with&amp;nbsp;international accounting standards (IFRS).&lt;br&gt;● Manage and execute the consolidation process, ensuring accurate aggregation of financial data for various entities and subsidiaries.&lt;br&gt;● Prepare accurate and timely monthly management reporting packs along with key&amp;nbsp;metrics.&lt;br&gt;● Collaborate with internal teams to gather financial data and ensure completeness and&amp;nbsp;accuracy.&lt;br&gt;● Conduct analysis to identify and explain significant variances in Financials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2) Data Analysis and Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Liaise with the data analytics team to automate financial reporting metrics /dashboards through reporting tools (Tableau / NetSuite analytics / Cursor)&lt;br&gt;● Ensure the integrity and consistency of financial data used across financial and&amp;nbsp;management reporting.&lt;br&gt;● Propose and implement process improvements to streamline reporting workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3) Audit Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Assist in preparing quarterly and annual financial statements in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;applicable accounting standards (IFRS).&lt;br&gt;● Collaborate with external auditors during the audit process, providing necessary&amp;nbsp;documentation and addressing audit findings.&lt;br&gt;● Manage audit timelines, deliverables, and key milestones, ensuring timely completion&amp;nbsp;of the audit process.&lt;br&gt;● Proactively identify, manage, and resolve audit challenges and potential roadblocks to&amp;nbsp;ensure an efficient and successful audit outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4) Financial project &amp;amp; Strategic support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Support the financial requirements of key strategic projects, including debt financing, due diligence, company valuation, and financial integrity and gap assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5) New Product Setup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Assess and anticipate potential accounting, compliance, and audit implications arising&amp;nbsp;from new products, identifying key risks and recommending appropriate mitigation&amp;nbsp;measures.&lt;br&gt;● Define and implement financial flows and reporting logic for new products.&lt;br&gt;● Perform accounting assessments for new products, ensuring alignment with applicable&amp;nbsp;accounting standards, regulatory requirements, and internal policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your expertise:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ACCA or equivalent certificate is a benefit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of experience in financial reporting, preferably in the financial industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in the financial services and banking sectors is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing end-to-end audit processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in preparing monthly, quarterly, and yearly management reporting pack. Also ensuring accurate consolidation of group financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with advanced excel and other financial reporting tools. Familiarity with AI or automation tools such as Cursor, Power BI is considered an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Experience in supporting accounting assessments of new product implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; Experience in Islamic financing and shariah compliance is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Arabic is an advantage&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Fraud Investigator for our Trust and Safety team. As a Fraud Investigator, you will be crucial in monitoring and investigating suspicious transactions and activities to help protect our company and our customers from financial losses and reputational damage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing on your proficiency in identifying potentially harmful activities through in-depth investigations and clear reporting, you will be responsible for collaborating with teams, implementing effective anti-fraud solutions, and elevating overall security posture to create unique experiences only Tamara can provide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a proven track record of analyzing complex data with precision, extracting valuable insights through keen observation, communicating clearly and persuasively, tailoring messages to diverse audiences in English, Arabic, and ultimately revolutionize the way millions of users shop, pay, and bank.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a driven, determined, curious team player, knowing that collective strength means we all win. With a positive outlook, you are solution-oriented–persevering regardless of circumstances, always finding a way through, no matter the challenges.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will effectively find a way to work with everyone through empathy and respect. You will be driven and comfortable with responding quickly with urgency, with the ability to change course without losing momentum and energy, resulting in great success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze transactions and activities to identify potential fraud, money laundering, or other criminal activities Utilize data analysis, statistical modeling, and fraud detection tools to identify suspicious patterns, trends, and anomalies in financial transactions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate suspicious activities and prepare detailed reports of findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other teams to implement fraud prevention measures and improve overall security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up-to-date with industry trends and developments in fraud prevention techniques and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support and guidance to other team members as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call the customers and Merchants frequently to verify the details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work a flexible schedule/shift/work area, including weekends, nights, and/or holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a related field or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Excel, SQL and Python is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3 years of experience in fraud prevention or investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and Arabic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of AML will lead and manage the overall operations, activities, and responsibilities of the AML/CTF Department, reporting administratively to the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) and functionally to the Audit Committee. The role is responsible for developing, implementing, and maintaining the company’s Anti-Money Laundering, Counter-Terrorist Financing, and Proliferation Financing (AML/CTF/PF) framework in Saudi Arabia. This includes ensuring compliance with the Saudi Anti-Money Laundering Law and its Implementing Regulations, SAMA requirements, SAFIU reporting obligations, and applicable Targeted Financial Sanctions requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of AML will work closely with business and control functions to identify and assess financial-crime risks, ensure that effective controls are implemented consistently across the company, remediate identified gaps, and promote a strong culture of AML/CTF/PF compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AML/CTF/PF Framework and Controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop, implement, monitor, and continuously enhance the company’s AML/CTF/PF framework and controls to ensure their effectiveness and alignment with applicable regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Oversight of AML/CTF/PF Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and oversee the AML/CTF Unit’s activities, ensuring that all responsibilities are performed effectively and that identified control or process deficiencies are addressed promptly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policies and Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop, maintain, and periodically review the company’s AML/CTF/PF policies, procedures, standards, and operating controls to reflect regulatory developments, emerging risks, and relevant industry practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise-Wide Risk Assessment:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the identification and assessment of money laundering, terrorist financing, and proliferation financing risks arising from the company’s customers, products, services, transactions, delivery channels, and geographic exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management and Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain effective relationships with key internal stakeholders and provide guidance and advice on AML/CTF/PF risks, regulatory requirements, new products, business initiatives, and control enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sanctions and PEP Screening:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee sanctions, Targeted Financial Sanctions, and politically exposed person screening controls, including alert investigation, escalation, decision-making, freezing measures, and regulatory reporting where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Board and Senior Management Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide the CEO and Audit Committee with regular reports on the company’s AML/CTF/PF risk exposure, control effectiveness, key performance indicators, material cases, regulatory developments, identified deficiencies, and the status of remediation actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management and Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain effective relationships with key internal stakeholders and provide guidance, awareness, and advice on AML/CTF/PF risks, requirements, and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Monitoring &amp;amp; Alert Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee transaction monitoring mechanisms ensuring effective rule tuning, threshold settings, and scenario management to minimize false positives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Suspicious Activity Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure that unusual activities are investigated appropriately and that suspicious transaction or activity reports are submitted accurately, confidentially, and within the applicable timelines to the Saudi Financial Intelligence Unit through official reporting channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary point of contact for AML/CTF/PF matters and coordinate timely, accurate, and complete responses to requests, inspections, and inquiries from SAMA, SAFIU, and other competent authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage and develop the AML/CTF team, establish clear responsibilities and performance expectations, and ensure the function has appropriate resources, knowledge, systems, and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 6 + years of relevant experience in AML/CTF, financial-crime compliance, regulatory compliance, or a related field, including experience in a leadership or management role under SAMA supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previously approved / pre-approved by SAMA is highly desirable, but not mandatory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the Saudi AML/CTF regulatory framework, SAMA requirements, SAFIU reporting obligations, Targeted Financial Sanctions, and relevant international standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in transaction monitoring, alert and case management, suspicious activity investigations, sanctions screening, and AML system capabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of money laundering, terrorist financing, and proliferation financing risks, typologies, red flags, and control practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, analytical, decision-making, communication, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle sensitive and confidential matters with sound judgment, independence, and integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certification, such as CAMS, an ICA qualification, or an equivalent financial-crime compliance certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Due to SAMA regulations we are looking to hire a saudi national in this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

