&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Merchant Acquisition Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; who will join our In-store Operations team and will be responsible for signing new businesses and inspecting our in-store marketing efforts at Tamara’s partner stores. The role involves being on the ground and visiting new and existing merchants. It’s ideal for an energetic individual who is eager to learn and grow in a dynamic start-up environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Merchant Outreach: Proactively identify and approach potential merchants in their physical store locations, introducing the company&#39;s services or products and explaining the benefits of partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship Building: Establish and nurture strong relationships with merchants, understanding their unique needs and challenges to position the company&#39;s offerings as valuable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-Site Demonstrations: Conduct in-person product or service demonstrations and address merchant concerns to secure new partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Intelligence Gathering: Collect and report valuable market insights, competitor activities and merchant feedback to inform company strategy and product development, including in-store materials visibility,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversion and Onboarding: Guide interested merchants through the application and onboarding process, ensuring a smooth transition and laying the groundwork for a successful long-term partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At a minimum, internship or co-op training experience in sales or business development with a maximum of 2 years of experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, capable of engaging with merchants and internal stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle confidential information with discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite; familiarity with CRM software is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, goal-oriented, and eager to learn about and grow within the BNPL sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable and resilient, with the ability to thrive in a high-growth, fast-paced industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player who takes initiative and brings a positive attitude to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KSA drivers license is a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Merchant Retention Lead owns the retention and reactivation of unmanaged SMB merchants across the UAE. This role leads a team of specialists who contact churned merchants to understand why they stopped transacting and resolve or escalate the issue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team also proactively monitors unmanaged merchants whose order volume is slowing down, identifies the reasons behind the decline, and provides the right support before they fully churn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Team leadership and execution:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and performance-manage a team of Specialists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team priorities, merchant portfolios, outreach targets, and follow-up SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear daily and weekly operating rhythm for calls, follow-ups, escalations, and performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor call quality, CRM updates, and action-plan execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure each merchant case has a clear churn or slowdown reason, next action, owner, and follow-up date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Churn and slowdown management&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outreach to churned merchants with no orders for a predetermined number of days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an early-intervention approach for unmanaged merchants whose transaction volume is slowing down&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team identifies the root cause behind churn or declining activity through structured merchant conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define action plans for each churn reason, including issue resolution, training, product support, or escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track merchants through the recovery journey and confirm whether they resume transacting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;SOPs, frameworks, and insights&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the team’s SOPs, call guides, churn-reason framework, escalation paths, and recovery playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear definitions and processes for churned, slowing-down, contacted, in-recovery, reactivated, and unresolved merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze churn and slowdown reasons to identify recurring patterns by merchant segment, issue type, and outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share merchant feedback and systemic problems with the relevant teams and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend improvements to products, processes, training, communications, or commercial policies based on merchant insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Cross-functional coordination&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Engineering, Care, Risk, Finance, Commercial, Onboarding, Training, and Operations teams to resolve merchant issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate blockers to the correct owner and follow through until resolution or a clear outcome is reached&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highlight repeated issues that affect multiple merchants and support the development of long-term fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear communication with stakeholders on recovery performance, risks, and support required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Performance management and reporting&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track team activity and outcomes, including contact rate, reason identification, follow-up completion, reactivation rate, and recovered transaction volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular reporting on churn reasons, slowing-down merchants, open blockers, and recovery actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review team performance and coach specialists based on quality, productivity, and merchant outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and timely CRM records for all merchant interactions and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in merchant success, retention, account management, customer success, sales, or a related function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading or coaching a customer-facing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build practical SOPs, frameworks, and action plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing performance through KPIs, operating cadences, and coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder-management and escalation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset and ability to identify patterns from merchant feedback and performance data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and follow-through on open merchant issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong CRM discipline and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, BNPL, e-commerce, or merchant acquiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SMB merchants in the UAE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in churn prevention, customer retention, or merchant reactivation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arabic language capability alongside professional English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Merchant Success Lead owns the Day 0–30 post-live health and early transaction performance of SMB merchants across the UAE. This role leads a team of&amp;nbsp; Merchant Success team members across Dubai, Sharjah, and Abu Dhabi and is accountable for ensuring merchants are operationally ready, properly trained, visibly set up, and supported to reach an impactful daily transaction volume&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Team leadership and coverage:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and performance-manage a team of Merchant Success team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set city-level territories, merchant portfolios, visit plans, and daily priorities based on volume, risk, and activation opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a field operating rhythm covering daily execution, weekly performance reviews, coaching, and quality checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct audits to improve merchant conversations and execution quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast capacity and rebalance workload to maintain SLA coverage across all assigned merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear onboarding, playbooks, and performance expectations for new team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Day 0–30 merchant health ownership&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Merchant Success execution from First Order Date until the merchant reaches a minimum threshold level of transactions or exits through an agreed recovery path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure internal health checks are completed for merchants below a minimum number of orders, covering online visibility, in-store readiness, widget setup, marketing kit status, operational blockers, and order volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure external health checks are completed for merchants, including merchant contact or field visits, training reinforcement, visibility checks, and recovery planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm every unresolved issue has a named owner, next action, and committed due date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor ageing merchants and intervene when cases are at risk of missing SLAs or remaining below the transaction threshold&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Performance management and reporting&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Merchant Success KPI dashboard and provide clear weekly performance reporting by city, team member, cohort, and issue type&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track leading and lagging indicators, including health-check SLA attainment, contact and visit completion, recovery rate, time to minimum transactions, merchant conversion, and CRM hygiene&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify underperformance early and implement coaching or corrective action plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze recurring blockers and recommend changes to processes, materials, training, CRM journeys, or product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reliable pipeline visibility and communicate risks, dependencies, and decisions to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Merchant Success Lead is expected to travel across select city footprints and maintain sufficient field presence to coach the team and understand merchant conditions firsthand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in merchant success, account management, field sales, retail operations, activation, or a related customer-facing function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of direct people-management experience, ideally leading a distributed or field-based team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage performance through KPIs, operating cadences, coaching, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, stakeholder-management, and escalation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing operational blockers and coordinating multiple teams to drive resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in the field and travelling regularly across Dubai, Sharjah, and Abu Dhabi&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and ability to turn performance data into priorities and actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership, attention to detail, and follow-through on time-sensitive SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coach non-technical merchant or retail staff on product usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Partner Onboarding Advisor is responsible for executing Tamara’s merchant onboarding steps end-to-end for assigned merchants—focusing on accuracy, SLA adherence, and a smooth merchant experience. The role owns KYB, compliance and fraud checks, integration coordination, and activating merchants/partners for go-live readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1) Merchant intake &amp;amp; case ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick up assigned merchants from the relevant queue/view, take ownership, and manage the case through activation/go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and work on support queues for merchants who are not live yet; action tickets promptly and correctly, ensure all actions/decisions are documented in internal notes, and communicate clearly and professionally with merchants throughout the full ticket lifecycle (updates, requests, and resolution).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make proactive follow-up calls with merchants that have pending actions (e.g., missing go-live requirements, pending integration steps on the merchant side, or pending contract signature) to unblock progress, reduce average time-to-go-live, improve conversion rates by increasing the % of merchants who complete pending actions and go live, and improve NPS by creating a more supportive onboarding journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2) KYB &amp;amp; document collection/validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate submitted documents (CR/Trade License/Freelancer certificate, ID, IBAN, VAT where applicable) and ensure they meet minimum validity and quality requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm consistency across documents and system fields (legal names, expiry dates, authorized signatory, entity type).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively follow up to request missing information, requirements, or documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3) Compliance &amp;amp; fraud checks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure required checks are completed and recorded per process; escalate unclear or exception cases via defined escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4) Integration &amp;amp; activation readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with relevant internal teams (e.g., Integrations, Risk/Compliance/Trust &amp;amp; Safety) to unblock merchants and progress integration/activation steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support merchants through blockers to go live via support queues and follow-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5) Support queues &amp;amp; KYB updates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work support queues to help merchants who are facing blockers to go live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate and process changes for merchants updating their KYB information, ensuring updates are correct and compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6) Merchant communication &amp;amp; follow-ups&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear, professional communication with merchants through approved channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A significant part of the role is calling merchants to follow up and request missing information/documents to keep cases moving within SLA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0–2 years experience in onboarding, operations, customer operations, compliance operations, KYC/KYB, or a similar process-driven role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and comfort working with checklists, evidence, and audit-ready documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage a queue and prioritize by SLA/impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and professional stakeholder management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with KYB/KYC concepts and screening/risk workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Salesforce (or similar CRM) for case management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fintech, payments, marketplaces, or regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;People Operations Associate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is Saudi Arabia’s first fintech unicorn and is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company by the Public Investment Fund (PIF), SNB Capital, &lt;a href=&quot;http://checkout.com/&quot;&gt;Checkout.com&lt;/a&gt;, amongst others. The company operates from its headquarters in Riyadh, with additional regional and global support offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Associate, you’ll be the first point of contact for employees throughout their journey with us—from pre‑boarding to off‑boarding. You’ll handle day‑to‑day HR operations, ensure full compliance with UAE labour legislation, and partner closely with our PRO, Finance, IT, and insurance providers. This role is ideal for an HR professional who loves process excellence, has a strong service mindset, and thrives in a multicultural environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pre‑boarding &amp;amp; On‑boarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end onboarding management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain E-files of all employees compliant with the internal policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect hiring documents, coordinate IT setup, and schedule orientation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with UAE PRO on entry visas, work permits, and Emirates ID issuance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare employee files in line with GDPR and local data‑privacy rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employee Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the HR help‑desk, responding to inquiries within 24 hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue HR letters, salary certificates, NOCs, and add dependents to visas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visas &amp;amp; Immigration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end‑to‑end Golden Visa applications for employees and dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor visa/EID/contract expiries, ensuring 100% timely renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage medical insurance enrolments, claims, deletions; reconcile monthly invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend benefit enhancements based on employee feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Off‑boarding&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect assets, deactivate system access, and complete visa cancellations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue end‑of‑service letters and final settlement instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Policy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep HR policies current with UAE labour law and DIFC/Free‑Zone updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain audit‑ready records and support external/internal audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in HR, Business Administration, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3 years in an HR operations or People Associate role within the UAE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grasp of UAE Labour Law, free‑zone regulations, and visa processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Experience in Payroll is highly desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with HRIS platforms (e.g., HiBob, SuccessFactors, BambooHR, Zoho people) and MS Office/Google Workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and organisational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, empathetic written &amp;amp; verbal communication (English a must; Arabic a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Service‑oriented mindset with the ability to juggle multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Golden Visa procedures and payroll coordination is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is a leading fintech platform in Saudi Arabia and the GCC region with a mission to help people own their dreams built on being simple, trusted, and everywhere our customers need us. Today, more than 25 million customers and over 130,000 partner merchants depend on Tamara every day for reliable financial solutions across retail, travel, education, healthcare, and beyond. Tamara is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company of the Public Investment Fund (PIF), and SNB Capital, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tamara is Saudi Arabia’s first fintech unicorn and is backed by Sanabil Investments, a wholly owned company by the Public Investment Fund (PIF), SNB Capital,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://checkout.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://Checkout.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Checkout.com&lt;/a&gt;, amongst others. The company operates from its headquarters in Riyadh, with additional regional and global support offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a People Business Partner for our People team. As a People Business Partner, you will be crucial in providing tactical and strategic consulting on people and organization development strategies in support of the business objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing on your proficiency in contributing to the development and implementation of HR policies and programs, you will be responsible for carrying out the following functional areas: employee relations consultation, policy interpretation and application, performance and compensation management consultation, talent management consultation to create unique experiences only Tamara can provide.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a proven track record of strong understanding of HR principles, practices, and regulations, excellent communication, interpersonal, problem-solving skills, and ultimately revolutionize the way millions of users shop, pay, and bank.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a driven, determined, curious team player, knowing that collective strength means we all win. With a positive outlook, you are solution-oriented–persevering regardless of circumstances, always finding a way through, no matter the challenges.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will effectively find a way to work with everyone through empathy and respect. You will be driven and comfortable with responding quickly with urgency, with the ability to change course without losing momentum and energy, resulting in great success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide HR partnership and support for strategic and tactical initiatives, including day-to-day HR assistance and strategy execution for assigned business groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster and maintain effective relationships with leaders and employees, offering guidance on HR and business issues at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and coach leaders and managers to achieve business objectives within the assigned populations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage employee relations and act as a change agent by implementing best practices and improving work relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
